※ A function with type parameters is written once and compiled once for each
※ set of types a call gives it, so there is no one function for something
※ outside to reach: the runtime's entry point, a constructor and a test are
※ each one thing the program has, and a template is none.

@[startup]
fn main(a: T') → u6:
    0u6
